        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Henry Wadsworth Longfellow, Dante Alighieri, St. Francis\n- Groups: Fireside Poets\n- Places: New England\n- Works: Divine Comedy, The Sermon of St. Francis\n- Topics: 19th-century American poetry, translation\n\nFacts:\n- Henry Wadsworth Longfellow was an American poet who lived from 1807 to 1882.\n- Henry Wadsworth Longfellow was one of the five Fireside Poets from New England.\n- The Fireside Poets were a group of 19th-century American poets associated with New England.\n- Henry Wadsworth Longfellow was the first American to translate Dante Alighieri's Divine Comedy.\n- The Sermon of St. Francis is a poem by Henry Wadsworth Longfellow.",
